{title: Auld Lang Syne}
{artist: Robert Burns (words), traditional (melody)}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 84}
{meta: public_domain Words by Robert Burns, 1788; traditional Scottish melody.}
{meta: source Burns's text as printed in The Scots Musical Museum, 1796.}
{meta: arrangement Original chord arrangement for Fretlight}

{start_of_verse}
Should [G]auld acquaintance [D]be forgot,
And [G]never brought to [C]mind?
Should [G]auld acquaintance [D]be forgot,
And [C]auld [D]lang [G]syne?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
For [G]auld lang syne, my [D]dear,
For [G]auld lang [C]syne,
We'll [G]tak a cup o' [D]kindness yet,
For [C]auld [D]lang [G]syne.
{end_of_chorus}
